          "title": "You'll want to know: desahogarse",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "desahogarse — \"to let off steam, to pour one's heart out\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Necesito hablar contigo para desahogarme. I need to talk to you to get it off my chest."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Desahogarse con alguien — to open up to someone. El desahogo is the relief it brings."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "desahogarse is built on ahogar \"to choke, to drown\" with the prefix des-: to stop choking. Ahogar comes from spoken Latin affōcāre, Latin offōcāre \"to choke\" (EtymDB), from faucēs \"throat\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
